        "issueId": "sah-237-sah-233",
        "text": "23/2 Caris - GCG report linked. Noting extraction rate issues have been resolved, however, will we address recommendations within the report: \n\n- Review the design of the slot hood for the sinks in both rooms. A longer single slot positioned closer to the lip of the sink height will be more effective in capturing VOC from cleaning tasks. This will also capture VOC before they reach the user’s breathing zone. Extending the slot to full sink width will increase the capture area. \n- Consider adding angled slots to the end of a remanufactured slot hood. This will induce airflow from the work surfaces on either side of the sinks, which will aid in the capture of VOC from containers placed there awaiting cleaning.",
