    "subject": "Current suspended light fixture height is not fit for purpose, as large materials are regularly transported from the Metalwork and Woodwork workshops to the Production & Assembly area. \n\n- This creates a risk of collision with the lights.\n\n- The air hose reel valve and hose, currently fixed to the underside of the concrete soffit, is not accessible without a ladder.\n\n- When in use, the hose will clash with the suspended light fixtures, creating operational and safety concerns.\n\n- Hanging GPO's not seen.\n\nMPX to review the current design and confirm proposed solution to ensure,\n\n- Adequate clearance for material movement, as high as possible, MPX to please confirm height.\n- Revised location or mounting strategy for the air hose reel regulator to allow safe, accessible use.\n- Coordination between lighting height and hose reel positioning to prevent clashes during operation.\n- Confirm suspended  GPOs, ensure they are setout at the perimeters to avoid clashing with the gantry.",
