    "subject": "Sheer and Blockout blind functionality",
    "detail": "In all dance studios staff noted that it is all or nothing with the sheer and blackout blinds – they are all down or all up. Staff wondered if there is the possibility for them for each blind to be controlled independently for more flexibility? – i.e. to block out excessive sun from Yagan square in the morning while still being able to have natural light coming through windows that look out onto Karak Walk, or to have natural light coming through the windows over the void space while having the blackout blinds down on the windows that look out to the north-south corridor in the black box when not in performance/presentation mode. On each control panel on the table (so not the wall switch) there is also an option for the blinds which might indicate that there is the possibility to have different presets?",
    "priority": "4 - Minor - Low Impact / Cosmetic",
