    "roomCode": "CC.1N.320\nCC.1N.219\nCC.1N.232\nCC.1N.241\nCC.1N.233\nCC.1N.234\nCC.1N.324",
    "roomName": "Dance Studios",
    "subject": "AV Screen Functionality",
    "detail": "We have 13 spaces fitted with Viscom AV systems controlling both a projector and a motorised screen across multiple space types (Dance, M&V Studios, Costume and others) It’s been noted in the Dance Studios that when the system is powered up, the screen automatically deploys. A common use case in these spaces is audio playback only, where a deployed screen is not required and is often undesirable. Feedback from Kynan (Dance) is that in any of the dance studios, simply playing music results in the projector screen coming down, which suggests this may be set as a default behaviour. Could this please be checked and confirmed:• Is this a programmable or configurable setting within the Viscom control logic?• Can the system be configured so audio-only use does not automatically deploy the screen/projector?• If so, the recommended default behaviour for all AV system in these spaces could be the same..For dance this is the biggest concern in 1N.219 and 1N.320 (White and Black presentation spaces) as there is no way to retract the screen once it is down other than powering down the room. This is not desirable for dance classes or presentation/showings. It will also be a problem for the M&V presentation studios.",
    "priority": "3 - Standard - Moderate Impact",
    "photoReference": "",
    "sourceCategory": "AV and IT",
    "category": "AV/IT",
