    "subject": "Incorrect placing of teaching station and/or cabling loom too short",
    "detail": "In a number of the WAAPA teaching spaces, most prominently those listed above, teaching stations have been incorrectly installed, either in the wrong location in the room or in such a way that the desk can only be facing the wall due to the shortness of the IT cabling loom leading from the wall to the desk.447 – teaching station on the wrong side of the room. Should be on the southern wall, adjacent to the board and projection screen and opposite the lecture recording camera, as per design. You can see in the photo that the camera looks over the presenter's shoulder. 312/313 – these looms are both exceptionally short and the desks can not be turned to face into the room. Positioning here is also questionable in relation to the teaching orientation. The front of the room is clearly to the south in both spaces. In 313, the desk is impeding a fire extinguisher and can't be moved because of the loom (WHS issue). 338/400/401 – loom too tight. Manageable for initial delivery but needs attention.",
