    "subject": "No Network Points for Plotter",
    "detail": "This device needs to be hard-wired to the ECU network to be deployed by staff & students. The device was initially intended for a different room, but various changes and access issues mean that the best spot for it is in the M44 Prototyping Lab. Unfortunately the nearest port is across the room. Ideally a port would be installed into the the wall near the printer, possibly through the spot that currently has a powerpoint which looks as if it goes through a channel to M45 (where there are numerous spare ports). As a back-up/shorter-term option, an extension cable could be run across the room above the door to plug into the wall-port that is behind the Bambu 3D printer (see photo). A very short term solution will be to manually drape an extension cable across the door. This will be implemented by us if we can locate a cable but it will look messy and potentially be a hazard. The short term solution could be to neatly dress this cable into the corners of the room. The best long term solution which hopefullly won't require too much renovation would be to provide a network port in the location of the nearest powerpoint.\nThe ideal longterm solution would be a new powerpoint and network port, somewhere in that corner.",
