    "roomName": "",
    "subject": "Curtain tracking following from the ceiling",
    "detail": "This is the second Ensemble room (the other being CC.1N.337) which has had the curtain track come away from the ceiling with the fixings tearing out. Both tracks VERY narrowly missed students when they came down, with the fallen track damaging a grand piano in 337, and the track falling today in 117 landing on the double bass as it was being played. NB: the damage to the double bass appears to be largely cosmetic as opposed to structural, but needs to be evaluated. There is now some concern that curtain tracking in other spaces may not have been adequately secured, which would pose some significant risk to staff and students. Perhaps the curtains can be taken down until all tracks have been checked as to their structural stability to ensure safety for those using the spaces.  WHS issue",
